<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina auctions 91-, 182-day T-Bills.</title>
<headline>Argentina auctions 91-, 182-day T-Bills.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina Tuesday auctioned 250 million pesos in 91-day Letes Treasury bills and $250 million in 182-day Letes, both at a cut-off yield of 5.9 percent, the Economy Ministry said.</p>
<p>There were 68 bids on the 91-day bills for a bid-to-cover ratio of 4.05 times and 77 bids for the 182-day bills for a bid-to-cover of 6.54 times.  </p>
<p>Market makers will be offered up to 10 percent more of both issues until 1700 local/2000 GMT Tuesday.</p>
<p>Settlement is due on June 20.</p>
<p>For more information see  ARG05 and  ARG06.</p>
<p>((-Gary Regenstreif, Buenos Aires newsroom, 541 318-0618))</p>
